# Streamlit Dashboard

- Use `streamlit-aggrid` for dataframe display via `_render_aggrid` (not `st.dataframe`).
- Size AgGrid columns with `flex`/`minWidth` and drop `autoSizeStrategy` from `GridOptionsBuilder.from_dataframe` so columns expand after the Streamlit iframe sizes (do not rely on `fitGridWidth` or removed `use_container_width`).
- Render Plotly charts with `st.plotly_chart(..., width="stretch")`.
- Flight-count charts should start the count axis at zero using `_start_flight_count_axis_at_zero`.
- Line charts should not show markers; keep daily date series complete with `_complete_daily_series`.
- Keep focus-airport maps fitted to the focus airport and destinations via `_map_center_zoom_from_coords` (use center/zoom, not bounds, so users can zoom out).
- Use the shared Top N control for route and arc counts instead of adding separate route-arc limits.
- Insight comparisons place new or increases on the left and drops or disappeared on the right across charts, maps, and tables.
- When dashboard chart behavior changes, update or add regression coverage in `tests/test_dashboard_chart_rules.py`.

# Dashboard layout

- `flight_dashboard.py` is entry only: `set_page_config`, `build_dashboard_context`, `dispatch_section`.
- Sidebar widgets live in `dashboard/sidebar.py`; section renderers take `DashboardContext` and use `ctx.field` directly (no unpacking).
- New sections go in `dashboard/sections/` and register in `dispatch_section`.
- Shared tab/chart logic goes in `dashboard/tab_charts.py` (or similar), not duplicated across sections.
- Section files over ~400 lines become a package: `__init__.py` for dispatch, one module per tab or mode.
- After structural changes, run `uv run pytest tests/test_dashboard_imports.py tests/test_dashboard_chart_rules.py -v`.
- Then **launch** the dashboard (`uv run streamlit run streamlit/flight_dashboard.py`) and smoke-test via the browser at the **Local URL** that process prints — do not reuse an existing localhost URL (another app may be on that port).
